The Quiet Below is a series of caverns that snake miles below the surface of the continent of [[Geography/index|Edan]]. No great civilizations lived there, and there are no known resources that couldn't be gathered closer to the surface, so rarely do people venture into the underground caves.

Superstitious people believe that it's harder for the God's blessings to reach you below the surface, and dangerous monsters lurk in the dark depths, so the only people who reside here are doing so to avoid the public eye. The hearsay is that travel below the surface of [[Færrin]] puts you out of reach of the gods, because the gods are from the sky, though no one has ever established it as fact. Almost nothing lives below but monsters, and there is no reason to mine when the same minerals can be had nearer the surface, so the only reason to go down is that you are not welcome above.

The Party came upon an entry point to the Quiet Below through a lift and staging area buried under [[Geography/Calaria/Hallia/index|Hallia]], a place evidently built and kept up by some clandestine group. Argyle felt his connection to the [[Judge of Ages|Judge]] grow faint as they descended, and wrote it in his notebook.
